kness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=805559#post805559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a 1950's Americana setting for Vampire: The Masquerade</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know I needed this until now. That sounds amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:40:09-08:00","id":808195,"title":"","content":"Mesopotamia, from the rise of the Sumerian City-States through the Late Bronze Age Collapse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T01:26:42-08:00","id":808513,"title":"","content":"So essentially, all of human history ever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> At least it's easy to make your own in the WoD. All you need is a book or two and wikipedia and you're golden.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:43:20-08:00","id":808636,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see Christianity of Poland era, when kingdom was formed. It was wery rural country with thick woods and forrests. It's perfect place for Red talons, plotting Shadow Lords with Get accents (Sygryda Storr\u00e5da, \u015awi\u0119tos\u0142awa was sister of polish king and very influent queen, besides many scandinavians visited Poland then so with them Get could visit caerns too - maby with not so friendly intentions<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). It was time for expansion, plotting and battles. In lupus garou eyes it could be time when similar apes gather together in woods, follow new strange rituals around cross shaped wood and deforestating their homes. Homid garou could see new enemy - church and religion, maby some conflicts around territories and septs, opportunities to manipulate human herd - lot of possibilities. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T15:02:10-08:00","id":809125,"title":"","content":"Oh!? Taisho Japan!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T18:33:45-08:00","id":809285,"title":"","content":"Would be interesting to see something running around the Stone Age just to see how something runs way back in the days; it's not a period you see often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T21:20:12-08:00","id":809355,"title":"","content":"The Hellenistic age would be fun- the squabbling Ptolemaic, Macedonian, and Seleucid kingdoms, an ascendant Carthage, and the rise of the vigorous Roman Republic to pre-eminence on the Italian peninsula. You'd get a vast geographic expanse and a wide range of major powers and societies, as well as a number of interesting mixtures/collisions of culture (well, mostly Graeco-Macedonian and Persian/Egyptian/Babylonian, but still) that provide plenty of fodder for vampiric conflict and drama (adapting to changing times or squabbling with the parasites hanging on to the newcomers). The vast scale of slavery and massive release of stored wealth following Alexander's conquests also afford plenty of interesting disruptions to the Cainite 'economy' as it were. Of course you'd sort of have to mutilate away a good part of the Setite and Assamite fluff, as their geographic identity would lock away the heartlands of the two greatest powers for much of the period (Egypt and Syria) from convenient, Clan-diverse play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10809,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","user":"Andkat","date":". 01-15-2016, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10809-andkat","name":"Andkat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:01:50-08:00","id":809670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andkat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=809355#post809355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hellenistic age would be fun- the squabbling Ptolemaic, Macedonian, and Seleucid kingdoms, an ascendant Carthage, and the rise of the vigorous Roman Republic to pre-eminence on the Italian peninsula. You'd get a vast geographic expanse and a wide range of major powers and societies, as well as a number of interesting mixtures/collisions of culture (well, mostly Graeco-Macedonian and Persian/Egyptian/Babylonian, but still) that provide plenty of fodder for vampiric conflict and drama (adapting to changing times or squabbling with the parasites hanging on to the newcomers). The vast scale of slavery and massive release of stored wealth following Alexander's conquests also afford plenty of interesting disruptions to the Cainite 'economy' as it were. Of course you'd sort of have to mutilate away a good part of the Setite and Assamite fluff, as their geographic identity would lock away the heartlands of the two greatest powers for much of the period (Egypt and Syria) from convenient, Clan-diverse play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about Egypt. Cairo by Night has a fairly detailed history and a lot of bits and pieces scattered here and there elsewhere through the book that give a picture of a Clan-diverse Egypt. Sure the Settites have got some powerful mojo, vertible serpent nests in a few places, but there are definitely other vamps out there. LOTS of them. How can you NOT have Greek vampires following Alexander? How can a Brujah of the period NOT want to spend just EVERY NIGHT in the Library of Alexandria. Unless, of course, the light of the Pharos burns vamps like daylight or something...<br /> <br /> There are definitely some ideas to work with in Veil of Night to allow for reconstruction of a pre-Roman, pre-Islamic Middle East. (Actually, there is some bits about Carthage in there as well.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:19:40-08:00","id":809691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus Smythe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=808195#post808195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mesopotamia, from the rise of the Sumerian City-States through the Late Bronze Age Collapse.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems very ambitious. Dark Ages, Victorian Era, Wild West.... they take on around a century each. Depending on how you slice it, you're talking about 900 years. Conservatively taking it from, say the rise of Uruk to the Assyrian conquest. Comparatively that's like having a sourcebook for, say, the entire time of Dark Ages until right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:30:16-08:00","id":809697,"title":"","content":"Id be happy with an exploration of any of it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9449-marcus-smythe","name":"Marcus Smythe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:47:58-08:00","id":809957,"title":"","content":"oh Prohibition? Which clans and tribes do you think were involved, think any supernaturals condoned prohibition? A lot of nutjobs thought it would make America a Paradise<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#878787\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;The reign of tears is over. The slums will soon be a memory. We will turn our prisons into factories and our jails into storehouses and corncribs. Men will walk upright now, women will smile and children will laugh. Hell will forever be for rent.&quot; Reverend Billy Sunday</span></span><br /> <br /> Think some wackjob from the Chorus or SOL might agree with his lunacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 01-15-2016, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T12:14:16-08:00","id":810320,"title":"","content":"I think Mage would make a grand Space Opera. But as this is Historicals, the period between 1763 and 1848 was truly wild.<br /> <br /> Ordinary people could travel beyond the Western World without sacrificing everything else in life.<br /> <br /> Many sites of classical antiquity in Greece, Egypt, Anatolia, and the Levant, are open to Westerners for the first time in centuries.<br /> <br /> Travel to China and India are more open then any time since classical antiquity.<br /> <br /> The Americas are more open to travel.<br /> <br /> The Pacific and the Southern Polar regions are being explored.<br /> <br /> Folklore and folk culture is being examined.<br /> <br /> Basic forms of government are transforming.<br /> <br /> The Arts are exploding.<br /> <br /> Science and Technology are jumping forward.<br /> <br /> It's a truly amazing period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:33:42-08:00","id":810509,"title":"","content":"I think that a vampire game set in 18th century France would be awesome. The extreme wealth and debauchery of the nobility, the opulence and style of Baroque and Rococo, the intrigues of the Frence court. All as a backdrop for the intrigues of vampiric politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:08:48-08:00","id":811999,"title":"","content":"I have always wanted to do a pirate Sabbat game during the Golden age of Piracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:21:23-08:00","id":812667,"title":"","content":"What will you do if your ships boarded during the day?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:20:48-08:00","id":813276,"title":"","content":"Victorian Age Fae, showing the transition from DA:Fae to C:TD, Werewolf 1776, Biblical Age Vampire (the era of Ashurbanipal) , Summer of Love Mage, 1920s Hunter (More like Hunters Hunted than HtR).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:23:22-08:00","id":813278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=812667#post812667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What will you do if your ships boarded during the day?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably have to deal with the ghoul crew, no pack of vampires is dumb enough to set sail by themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T04:28:26-08:00","id":813280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=811999#post811999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always wanted to do a pirate Sabbat game during the Golden age of Piracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://thevampireblog.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/884.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://jenniferhwilliams.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/05/1083.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thevampireblog.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/884.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> Blog | Jennifer H. Williams | + The Vampire Blog </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://thevampireblog.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/884.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://thevampireblog.org/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/884.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:52:59-08:00","id":813526,"title":"","content":"My top pick would be Jazz Age Vampire, centered on the US Eastern Seaboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T11:01:45-08:00","id":814932,"title":"","content":"The most obvious settings are:<br /> 1. Gothic England, i.e. 19th-20th century. Yes, there technically are Victorian Age books, but they are about as shovelware as you get. I want quality material.<br /> 2. WWII. The event of such massive importance is woefully overlooked in WoD.<br /> 3. French revolution and surrounding periods. The march of progress and political ideas of freedom against blood monarchy and feudalism. Sounds familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-23-2016, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T11:04:14-08:00","id":814940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=809285#post809285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be interesting to see something running around the Stone Age just to see how something runs way back in the days; it's not a period you see often.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem with this and other antiquity suggestions is that they can't work in Vampire because of the Generations. Vampires were physical gods controling humanity's dreams and bringing chimerical dragons into reality at that point, so the game would be nothing like VtM or even Dark Ages. It would be like Nobilis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-23-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T11:08:13-08:00","id":814942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=811999#post811999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always wanted to do a pirate Sabbat game during the Golden age of Piracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Why wouldn't a vampire get on a highly flammable vessel with a tiny, unreplenishable herd, with which you can only interact when the highly flammable vessel is full of torches. And I hope you've brought your Auspex friend along, so he can spot ships for you to attack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2347,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","user":"Mahasamatman","date":". 01-23-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2347-mahasamatman","name":"Mahasamatman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2347_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:04:55-08:00","id":815022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=814940#post814940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem with this and other antiquity suggestions is that they can't work in Vampire because of the Generations. Vampires were physical gods controling humanity's dreams and bringing chimerical dragons into reality at that point, so the game would be nothing like VtM or even Dark Ages. It would be like Nobilis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite agree. It takes time for Vampires to get to that power level.<br /> You could absolutely play in a time when the oldest Vampires are equivalently nowadays Elders. And the players might be low generation, but they still start out as neonates. If the game doesn't incorporate time jumps, then there is no reason for it to be too different from any other setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T17:42:14-08:00","id":815136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=814942#post814942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. Why wouldn't a vampire get on a highly flammable vessel with a tiny, unreplenishable herd, with which you can only interact when the highly flammable vessel is full of torches. And I hope you've brought your Auspex friend along, so he can spot ships for you to attack <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a <b>Sabbat</b> pirate game :P You know the guys who whack potential recurits over the head with a shovel, and dance and jump over fires. Besides when it comes to herd, what sort of sabbat vampire pirate would you be if you didn't come into town and take whom ever you wanted. <br /> <br /> Of course, like with mortal pirates, vampiric piracy isn't to last that long either. But I thought with the ship being your pack, and the big governments of Europe repersenting the Camerilla, it could be fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T21:31:04-08:00","id":815241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahasamatman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=814940#post814940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem with this and other antiquity suggestions is that they can't work in Vampire because of the Generations. Vampires were physical gods controling humanity's dreams and bringing chimerical dragons into reality at that point, so the game would be nothing like VtM or even Dark Ages. It would be like Nobilis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the second city still had Vampires of Gen 4-11. They didn't survive the flood of course. There were high generation vampires through all of history, their weaker blood meant that they generally didn't make it past a couple centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T22:23:39-08:00","id":815258,"title":"","content":"The fact that 14th and 15th generation vampires seem to be a product of the 20th century, with the Curse of Caine bottoming out at 13th generation from the 19th century back to the Middle Ages would tend to argue against that. It might not have been possible to embrace vampires beyond the 4th or 5th generations back in the days of the First City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:24:34-08:00","id":819940,"title":"","content":"A 1920's pulp adventure Mage book would be neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T01:24:45-08:00","id":823156,"title":"","content":"A Vampire chronicle during the Bronze Age in the Middle East and Mediterranean. That would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:13:56-08:00","id":824412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=823156#post823156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire chronicle during the Bronze Age in the Middle East and Mediterranean. That would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, you might want to trim that down a bit. That's centuries upon centuries of time and dozens up dozens of cultures. That's like saying, I want a setting that covers from 500 AD until now. Is there any specific group/era you want to hit? The Time of the Seal Peoples? (That covers the Trojan War, serious issues for the Hittite Empire, some major crap going down in Canaan and enough trouble to even rattle Egypt. And that's not even trying to cover the Western Mediterranean or Mesopotamia/Persia proper...) And here are TONS of points in time like that. (How about the rise of the Mittani? The Etruscans and Celts and Celtiberians over next to those poor little put upon Latin folks? Everything going on in N. Africa west of Egypt (and that's going to be a hard row to hoe finding sources)? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T18:16:21-08:00","id":824720,"title":"","content":"The Old Testament era would be an interesting setting, especially for Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T13:03:35-07:00","id":851305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=804854#post804854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would pledge an ungodly amount of money for a Dark Ages: Wraith book to finally see the light of day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen Brother!!! Not sure how much id pledge having... limited means... but I like the idea<br /> <br /> Oh thoughts on prohibition? How involve you think supernaturals were with either bringing it about or illegal alchahol trafficing? <br /> <br /> Could see some extremist CoG or GlassWalkers working to aid and abbet it thinking that the wyrm more easily preys on the mind of intoxicated humans...<br /> <br /> Not sure on other supernaturals<br /> <br /> but have to be some even some wraiths who got suckered by speeches like.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#878787\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;The reign of tears is over. The slums will soon be a memory. We will turn our prisons into factories and our jails into storehouses and corncribs. Men will walk upright now, women will smile and children will laugh. Hell will forever be for rent.&quot; </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I find it difficult to understand how otherwise sane people bought absurd speeches like this but... it happened...</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T19:38:19-07:00","id":851533,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness set in the Comunist russia, Spy Games and such..Oh my god i need a technocracy game set in the Cold War era..Cuba, USA, Russia, Kennedy !!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T20:01:46-07:00","id":851541,"title":"","content":"I think a post war/early cold war setting would be cool. Thule society members being brought to the states in a occult paperclip style operation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:27:10-07:00","id":851765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=851541#post851541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a post war/early cold war setting would be cool. Thule society members being brought to the states in a occult paperclip style operation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or something more like the Israeli Nazi hunters, since there was a lot of Nephandi stuff going on. Enough for a truce and working alliance (or at least non-interference) between the Traditions and Technocracy. <br /> <br /> Combine that with the disintegration of said arrangement (kinda like the Western powers and Russia) and the Union's shift into the Pogrom that would dominate policy through the Cold War era...<br /> <br /> Teams of mages from either side hunting renegade Nazi Nephandi, bumping into each other, some of the mages being former allies but now by the lights of their respective leadership the relationship is now supposed to be hostile... <br /> <br /> Oh, and then Operation Paperclip style operations would take on a completely different character if they are rescuing <i>Nephandi</i>. How does a Nazi Nephandi hunter of either side respond if they find out that someone in their sect is doing <i>that</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:43:39-07:00","id":851984,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a setting for Europe and the Middle East during the Black Death. Or when the French Revolution kicked in since it did strike a blow against both the Toreador and the Silver Fangs (they were a big sore about it in the revised tribebook). This could be a way to save Derrick zeal's lover and keep his project on vampire genealogy going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T00:26:50-07:00","id":852268,"title":"","content":"Well the Viking Age could be interesting. After the collapse of Rome and the chaos of the tribe movement something like a civilisation is showing their first leafs....and boom Vikings all over the place. <br /> You can put Gangrel, Brujah and Werewolves on the dragon boats.<br /> I personally would make that an ancillae game and the PC must hold on to their territories and wealth. Or a nice Werewolf game where it's the Get vs. Whoever lives in the areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T00:52:54-07:00","id":852277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meldok</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/804492-eras-of-darkness-any-historical-setting-you-would-like-to-explore?p=852268#post852268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Viking Age could be interesting. After the collapse of Rome and the chaos of the tribe movement something like a civilisation is showing their first leafs....and boom Vikings all over the place.<br /> You can put Gangrel, Brujah and Werewolves on the dragon boats.<br /> I personally would make that an ancillae game and the PC must hold on to their territories and wealth. Or a nice Werewolf game where it's the Get vs. Whoever lives in the areas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We are actually playing a chronicle where we are a pack of Get vikings exploring the American continents in the 800's AD",